#
# Generated 2026-09-27, during the Phase 1 eval run — per the session brief,
# this is documentation only: apply it once the eval finishes and
# services/vocabulary_ladder/asset_pipeline.py / exercise_renderer.py can be
# touched again. Verify it still applies cleanly first (`git apply --check`)
# since other Phase 1 work may have landed on these two files meanwhile.
#
# Prerequisites before this patch does anything:
#   1. migrations/exercise_gen_bundle_prompts_draft.sql applied, with
#      `is_active = true` on the rows for the languages being tested.
#   2. VOCAB_LADDER_BUNDLE_MODE set to "shadow" (compare-only) or "on"
#      (authoritative) — default "off" makes both hunks below no-ops.
#
# What each hunk does
# --------------------
# asset_pipeline.py (TASK-815 — generation):
#   Adds a `BundleGenerator` call before the existing per-generator fan-out
#   in `_generate_for_sense_impl`. Only attempted on a full, unscoped regen
#   (`levels is None`) — TASK-811's level-scoped regen keeps using the
#   legacy path unconditionally, on purpose (see the added comment). In
#   "shadow" mode the bundle call still runs and is logged, but
#   `variant_results` is populated by the untouched legacy fan-out. In "on"
#   mode `variant_results` comes from `bundle_result.to_variant_results()`
#   and the legacy fan-out is skipped entirely. Step 4 (validate/store) is
#   UNCHANGED — both paths populate `variant_results` in the exact same
#   `{(prompt_type, variant_key): value}` shape it already reads.
#
# exercise_renderer.py (TASK-816 — render-time judges):
#   `build_rows` gains an eager pre-pass, `_gather_bundle_judge_requests`,
#   that re-derives the SAME candidate lists the 6 direct judge call sites
#   (L1 l1_distractor, L3 cloze, L5/L8 collocation, L6/L7 sentence_validity)
#   already build, across every (variant, level), and makes ONE
#   `BundleJudge.judge_bundle()` call before the render loop starts. The
#   render loop tags each level/variant with `self._current_variant_key` /
#   `self._current_level` (instance state, like the existing
#   `self.last_skips`) so the 6 call sites can look up their precomputed
#   verdict by the same `f'{variant}:L{level}'` request_id the gather step
#   used, WITHOUT a signature change to any renderer method. A cache miss
#   (bundle mode off, or this request wasn't gathered) falls through to the
#   original direct judge call, byte-for-byte unchanged.
#
# Known limitation — NOT wired by this patch
# -------------------------------------------
# The `synonym_antonym_match` (relation) and `particle_selection` (particle)
# judge axes are fully implemented and tested in
# `services/vocabulary_ladder/bundle/judge.py` (BundleJudge.judge_bundle
# already resolves `requests.relation` / `requests.particle` and falls back
# correctly), but `_gather_bundle_judge_requests` above does NOT populate
# them, and `_render_llm_types` / the typed generators'
# (`asset_generators/syn_ant.py`, `asset_generators/particle_selection.py`)
# `render()` methods are not modified here. Reason: `SynonymAntonymGenerator
# .render()` runs an embedding band-check (`sense_neighbours.band_check_foils`,
# a real DB call) BEFORE building its judge candidate list, and reproducing
# that pre-filter in the eager gather step — so the bundle-judged foil set
# matches what today's lazy path would have judged — needs either porting
# the band-check into the gather step or factoring `render()` so its
# pre-filter can run standalone before the eager pass. Wiring relation/
# particle without that would silently judge a different (unfiltered) candidate
# set than production does today, which is exactly the kind of quality
# regression ADR-028 says must not happen. Land the band-check port as a
# follow-up before enabling the relation/particle axes in "on" mode; "off"
# and "shadow" modes are unaffected either way since neither axis is
# gathered, so no fallback path is exercised for them yet.
#
# Testing performed before this patch was written (does not require applying it)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tests/test_bundle_flags.py, test_bundle_mapping.py, test_bundle_generator.py,
# test_bundle_judge.py — 36 tests, all passing, no live LLM/DB calls (see
# `PYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest tests/test_bundle_*.py -q`).
